config {
  type: "assertion",
  tags: ["cm360", "monitoring"],
  description: "cm360_reachv2 must hold one row per date + advertiser + campaign. The uniqueKey assertion on fct_cm360_reach_daily CANNOT catch this -- the mart groups by exactly those three columns, so duplicate source rows are summed into one before the assertion ever sees them."
}

-- An assertion FAILS if it returns rows. Empty result = healthy.
--
-- THIS EXISTS BECAUSE THE MART'S OWN ASSERTION IS BLIND TO IT, and that
-- was learned the expensive way on 2026-11-16.
--
-- stg_cm360_reach was repointed to cm360_reachv2 on 11-11 and its
-- largest-wins QUALIFY was taken out, on the stated reasoning that
-- fct_cm360_reach_daily asserts uniqueKey on date + advertiser_id +
-- campaign_id and would turn the workflow red if the source ever started
-- appending. That reasoning was wrong. The mart is
--
--   SELECT date, advertiser_id, campaign_id, SUM(impressions), ...
--   GROUP BY 1, 2, 3
--
-- so two source rows on one key collapse into one mart row with their
-- metrics ADDED. The key is unique by construction and the assertion
-- passes on every run. Nothing can make it fail.
--
-- WHAT THAT COST. CM360 resumed on 11-16 after five days frozen and
-- re-appended its window instead of replacing it. 4,429 rows for 4,390
-- keys -- 39 duplicated keys, all pairs, all on 11-07 to 11-10. The two
-- copies are the same campaign-day read twice, about 0.2% apart. Summed:
--
--   zi            clickuri raport   corect    impresii raport   corect
--   2026-11-07    20,310            19,186    8,888,213         6,455,576
--   2026-11-08    21,406            19,592   10,006,582         6,856,127
--   2026-11-09    31,338            20,997   10,770,170         7,030,879
--   2026-11-10    35,035            27,115   10,653,263         7,244,293
--
-- Clicks up to 49% high, impressions up to 53%, and clicks_check is what
-- v_campaign_daily publishes as THE CM360 click count. Four days of
-- reporting were wrong with every assertion green.
--
-- THE LESSON IS GENERAL. A uniqueKey assertion on a mart that aggregates
-- tests the GROUP BY, not the data. Wherever the source grain and the
-- mart grain are the same columns, the guard has to read the source.
-- assert_cm360_site_creative_grain is the same shape and caught its
-- source on the same morning, because it reads the grain rather than
-- the mart.

SELECT
  date,
  CAST(advertiserId AS STRING) AS advertiser_id,
  CAST(campaignId   AS STRING) AS campaign_id,
  'duplicate date + advertiser + campaign in cm360_reachv2' AS problem,
  COUNT(*) AS rows_affected
FROM ${ref({ schema: constants.DATASETS.cm360, name: "cm360_reachv2" })}
GROUP BY date, advertiserId, campaignId
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
